(** fuzz_rate's compiled builder leaves pp_bytes at pp. For four inputs (Pod/Sat.v's W1, the `role-master` seed of
    fuzz_role, W7 with all three property kinds, W8 with a corruption, and T4 at every bound), each after fuzz_rate's
    7 header bytes (flags, mask, buflen, other: 0 here), the 19744 bytes the compiled code of LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput
    wrote at pp, read at its second malloc call (the one in fuzz_dup: plain 0x141e0, UBSan 0x14208) by running it in
    an RV64GC emulator, are written below as their non-zero runs; the plain and the UBSan image wrote the same bytes,
    and the same bytes as fuzz_role's images (fuzz_role's RoleBin.v: the same sha256). Each lemma checks by
    computation that they are [pp_bytes] of the record [pod_build] makes of the input after the header bytes, and
    that pod_build reads that input to its end, as the code did (it read all 20, 20, 22 and 304 bytes of the harness
    input). A witness, at the real instance, that the Layout text is the memory the walk of the builder must reach.
    Statement text and computation only.

    The emulator: unicorn 2.1.1 (RISC-V 64), in docker image rl3-check:1 (python:3.12-slim with pip unicorn==2.1.1,
    pyelftools, capstone), running the emulator script of fuzz_role's RoleBin.v, unchanged, with fuzz_rate's
    addresses (each checked against the symbol table at load): entry 0x12fc0 / 0x12fe0, stop 0x141e0 / 0x14208,
    malloc 0x16694 / 0x16a7c; malloc,
    memset, memcpy, strlen and strcmp are modelled as their C meaning, the UBSan build's pod_write_ent (0x14a18) runs
    as compiled; any other block, a trap, a fault or a read past the input stops the run as an error (none occurred).
    Images: the unstripped twins of the pinned fuzz_rate.plain and fuzz_rate.ubsan (sha256 4ecf851e..., 593a406e...).
    Command: `docker run --rm -v <script directory>:/check -v <the unstripped images' directory>:/elf:ro -w /check
    rl3-check:1 python3 rate_bin.py`. *)
From Stdlib Require Import ZArith List Lia Bool.
From LinuxProcessSemantics.LinuxProcessSem Require Import BvBase.
From OSSVerify.Proofs.reac_pw.fuzz_rate.lib.Pod Require Import Cursor Model Layout Sat.
Import ListNotations.
Open Scope Z_scope.

(** The byte list of length n with the runs (offset, bytes) and 0 elsewhere (runs in increasing order, disjoint). *)
Fixpoint expand_from (pos : Z) (n : nat) (runs : list (Z * list Z)) : list Z :=
  match runs with
  | [] => repeat 0 n
  | (o, bs) :: runs' =>
      repeat 0 (Z.to_nat (o - pos)) ++ bs ++
      expand_from (o + Z.of_nat (length bs)) (n - Z.to_nat (o - pos) - length bs) runs'
  end.
Definition expand (n : nat) (runs : list (Z * list Z)) : list Z := expand_from 0 n runs.

